Exercise: sa-firewalld-review (chapter 20 lab)

servera is the web server and serverb is the partner that may use it.
Work with sudo or as root. Do not stop or disable firewalld.

On servera
 1. Install httpd, start and enable it. The home page
    /var/www/html/index.html contains the line: Welcome to servera
 2. httpd must also listen on ports 8080 and 9000
    (a file in /etc/httpd/conf.d/ with two Listen lines).
 3. Create the permanent zone partners with serverb's address as its source
    (172.25.250.11 on the course network, whatever getent hosts serverb shows
    on your lab). The zone allows:
      - the service http
      - a service of your own named portal, defined for 9000/tcp
      - a forward of port 8081 to port 8080
 4. The default zone (public) must NOT allow http, 8080 or 9000.
 5. Everything must survive a reload: use --permanent and --reload.

Check from serverb
 6. curl http://servera/ , http://servera:9000/ and http://servera:8081/
    work from serverb. From workstation they should be rejected.

On workstation
 7. Fill in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-firewalld-review
